CRASH-11: index the averaged node depths by reported node, in user units

Since 5.3.0 (commit 7266536f, #188) output_saveAvgResults() updated each
node's "Reported Max Depth" from AvgNodeResults[i] for every node i, but
AvgNodeResults holds one entry per reported node, in reported-node order.
With [REPORT] NODES listing a subset the loop read past the end of the block
(heap-buffer-overflow) and credited reported nodes' depths to other nodes.
The averages also hold node_getResults() values, already in user units, and
were multiplied by UCF(LENGTH) again (SI depths x 0.3048). Walk the reported
nodes with their own counter, drop the second conversion, and give
unreported nodes the point depth that 5.2.4 used for all nodes. US-unit
projects that report every node get bit-identical results.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CRASH-11_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/output.c b/src/legacy/engine/output.c
index f57370e..f408d6a 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/output.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/output.c
@@ -906,7 +906,7 @@ void output_updateAvgResults()
 
 void output_saveAvgResults(FILE* file)
 {
-    int i, j;
+    int i, j, k;
 
     // --- examine each reportable node
     for (i = 0; i < NumNodes; i++)
@@ -922,9 +922,13 @@ void output_saveAvgResults(FILE* file)
     }
 
     // --- update each node's max depth and contribution to system storage
+    //     (AvgNodeResults holds reported nodes only, already in user units)
+    k = 0;
     for (i = 0; i < Nobjects[NODE]; i++)
     {
-        stats_updateMaxNodeDepth(i, AvgNodeResults[i].xAvg[NODE_DEPTH] * UCF(LENGTH) / Nsteps);
+        if ( Node[i].rptFlag ) stats_updateMaxNodeDepth(i,
+            AvgNodeResults[k++].xAvg[NODE_DEPTH] / (double)Nsteps);
+        else stats_updateMaxNodeDepth(i, Node[i].newDepth * UCF(LENGTH));
         SysResults[SYS_STORAGE] += (REAL4)(Node[i].newVolume * UCF(VOLUME));
     }
 
